+## Session name resolution and local read summaries (partial)
+
+`internal/sessquery.Reader.Resolve` composes the persisted session repositories
+and the accepted state projector. It follows v0.5.0 §2.3: exact local live name,
+exact live name in allowlisted learned peer indexes, exact UUID, then not found.
+ASCII folding detects collisions; a unique case variant is not an exact match.
+`Repository.Resolve` now applies that same exact-name rule to its local tier.
+Peer source IDs are distinct from winning owner IDs. Duplicate observations of
+one session ID do not create a name ambiguity. Peer-source ties use bytewise host
+ID order; distinct folded-name session IDs refuse with `name_ambiguous`.
+
+`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event chains
+through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the derived identity,
+provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role, checkpoint ID, conflicts,
+and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List order is bytewise session ID;
+`InspectLocal` retains access to parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics.
+Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions
+remain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading never
+repairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership change.
+
+These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result renderer.
+Host display names, checkpoint creation time/age, workspace observations,
+capability observations, process liveness and per-peer sync timestamps still
+need their observation owners. Unknown ownership stays unknown.
+`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List` and the
+existing `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session without owner
+facts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields. No owner is invented
+and no doctor/provider/platform capability is advertised. Peer indexes and the
+allowlist are trusted inputs from upstream owners; these entries do not prove
+mesh authentication, completeness, freshness, or cross-peer lease union.
+
+TASK-260830-21gygk remains partial: qualified-selector syntax, target and
+precedence await the existing product decision. Unqualified strings containing
+`@` or `/` currently follow ordinary not-found matching; those tests are not an
+approved qualified-selector contract. The traceability and remaining bounds are
+in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md). No additional
+normative section is marked implemented by this partial work.
