+# TASK-260830-21gygk: bounded implementation evidence
+
+Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.5.0,
+commit `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`, embedded document SHA-256
+`562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a`.
+Full task scope remains §2.3, §5.1–5.2, §5.7, §14.4. This file records partial
+implementation; it does not change the normative ownership registry or task AC.
+
+## Acceptance rows
+
+**2 of 5 AC rows driven in full at the library boundary; 3 of 5 partially driven.**
+The five rows are the original task's selector resolution, ambiguity, list
+summaries, status summaries, and deterministic sorting, as in its prior stop-line
+packet. **0 of 5 rows accepted for public CLI delivery.** Tests remain uncommitted
+in the managed Story until the authorized board handoff/checkpoint flow; this
+packet cannot satisfy a requirement for committed/accepted test evidence.
+
+| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Selector resolution | `Reader.Resolve`; retained `Repository.Resolve` | `TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`, `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` | Partial: local exact name, allowlisted learned exact name, UUID and not-found order; qualified syntax/target/precedence unresolved. No attach/resume/chooser implementation or peer transport/authentication claim. |
+| Ambiguity | `Reader.Resolve` → `matchName`; `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity` | Driven: local and cross-peer ASCII-fold collisions refuse, one replicated identity is not two sessions, unique case variants do not resolve. Peer indexes and allowlist are trusted upstream inputs; no claim of freshness or identity attestation. |
+| List summaries | `Reader.List` → `Repository.ListSessions` → `Projector.Project` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed` | Partial: real identity, provider, owner/lease/local role where known, state, newest checkpoint ID, parked reason/retry. Missing §14.4 supplemental observation fields and public rendering remain pending. |
+| Status summaries | `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` → `Projector.Project`; `Reader.InspectLocal` | Same list tests; `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` | Partial: named/UUID healthy status and explicit local parked/tombstoned ID inspection. Closed CLI summary cannot encode unknown ownership. No fabricated host, capability, workspace, process, checkpoint time or sync observations. |
+| Stable sorting | `Reader.List`; `Reader.Resolve` → `peerCandidates` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity` | Driven: bytewise session ID order, deterministic bytewise peer-source tie break, permutation/duplicate-peer-allowlist stability. Tie break selects a source index, not an owner, latest state, or mutation route. |
+
+## Refusal and recovery coverage
+
+| Gate | Real entry test | Attack |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Folded-name ambiguity | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions` | N-collision-pair permits exactly two colliding identities. |
+| Exact-name admission | Same, plus `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` | N-case-variant and N-repository-case-variant admit one non-exact selector. |
+| Live eligibility | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt` | N-parked-id and N-tombstoned-id admit one excluded identity. |
+| Peer allowlist | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-unlisted-peer reads one unlisted identity. This proves filtering of the input allowlist, not authentication of that allowlist. |
+| Duplicate learned index | Same | N-duplicate-peer admits duplicates for one host ID. |
+| Read failure propagation | Same | N-read-failure-fallback treats repository-path failure as empty. Missing learned index, nil known index, missing root, and non-directory root are separately driven. |
+| Projection failure propagation | `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure` | N-projection-failure-fallback omits one invalid projection. |
+
+The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an isolated source
+copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw process exits and named failed
+tests, then restores and verifies the copied bytes. It has before/after green
+controls, a not-applied control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two
+prove no behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are attached on the
+task, rather than hard-coding a green claim in this file. No source-text gate was
+introduced, and this map is not itself an enforcement census.
+
+The read entry points perform no durable writes. The crash test interrupts the
+real repository create after record installation, inspects the parked projection,
+retries the byte-identical create through its owner, and observes the healed read.
+Repeated lists return identical values. This establishes read idempotency and
+composition with existing recovery, not a new crash protocol.
+
+Additional bounds: reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an
+atomic repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer acquisition,
+cross-peer lease union and differing replicated views are not measured. The
+repository/projector own record/event admission and validation. No new external
+provider, filesystem durability, terminal, RPC or CLI capability is attested.
+
+## Stop-The-Line dependency
+
+The existing qualified-selector question is unanswered. An approved contract must
+name syntax, source-peer versus winning-owner target, and precedence/ambiguity
+interaction. No guessed `name@host`, `host/name`, parser flag or qualification
+fallback is introduced. Tests with those strings merely exercise unqualified
+not-found behavior; they are not qualification fixtures.
+
+Public summary composition must obtain required facts from their observation
+owners. In particular, a valid event-free Session Record projects empty owner,
+lease and local role, while the pinned closed CLI SessionSummary mandates all
+three. `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` reproduces that mismatch
+through `Reader.List` and `cliresult.New`. Retain unknown facts and the internal
+projection until the authoritative public representation/observation integration
+is available; do not synthesize a success-shaped owner. This is a concrete bound
+on partial summary delivery, not a claim that writing a renderer is impossible.
